course: dictionary
lesson: 5807
title: Magical: real magic or just wonderful?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a first meaning and a second meaning. Magical is one of them. The first meaning is made by magic or having magic powers, like a magical sword in a fairy tale. The clues around the word tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «The scary wood has turned white and magical.» The wood is not really magic. Before, it was scary; now, after the snow, it looks so lovely that it feels special. The clue is the change from scary to beautiful, so magical here means wonderful.
explain: Magical can also describe a feeling or a time. «Christmas morning felt magical» does not mean there were spells. It means the day was so special that it felt like magic. Ask yourself: is there real magic here, or is it just very lovely?
fact: Magical is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a magical sword, a magical place, a magical evening.
fact: Magical has three forms: magical, more magical, most magical.
fact: «Magical» means made by magic or having magic powers, like a magical cloak or wand.
fact: «Magical» can also mean wonderful and special, so lovely it feels like magic.
fact: Things that look magical, like a rainbow or a magnet, have real explanations in science.
exercise: «The scary wood has turned white and magical.» In this sentence, magical means | *Wonderful and special, so lovely it feels like magic | Full of sharp, stinging nettles | Able to cast spells on other people | Hard and very heavy
exercise: «The unicorn lived in a magical forest where the trees could sing.» What does magical mean here? | Very tall and thin | Covered in snow | Noisy and crowded | *Made by magic, with magic powers
exercise: Which sentence uses magical to mean wonderful and special? | *«We had a magical evening under the stars.» | «The magical cloak made her invisible.» | «The magical wand glowed blue.» | «The magical sword was kept in a box.»
test: Magical has a second meaning. What is it? | *Wonderful and special, so lovely it feels like magic | Happy and loud | Very old and dusty | Strong enough to lift a car
test: What is magical thinking? | Dreaming about a unicorn at night | Thinking very hard about a maths sum | Wishing for a bike, then buying one | *Believing that thoughts alone make things happen
exam: How can you work out the meaning of magical in «a magical evening»? | Guess a random meaning without looking at the sentence | Skip the word and never come back to it | Look only at the small word a before it | *Use the clues: an evening that is lovely and special, so magical means wonderful
